# ============================================================================
# CodeQL Execution Mode Configuration
# ============================================================================
# The tool automatically selects execution mode based on this setting:
#
# LOCAL MODE: Set CODEQL_CLI_PATH to use locally installed CodeQL
#   - Faster startup (no Docker overhead)
#   - Requires CodeQL Bundle installation
#
#   IMPORTANT: You MUST download CodeQL Bundle (NOT just CLI):
#   1. Visit: https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases
#   2. Download the bundle for your platform:
#      - Windows: codeql-bundle-win64.tar.gz
#      - Linux: codeql-bundle-linux64.tar.gz
#      - macOS: codeql-bundle-osx64.tar.gz
#   3. Extract to a folder (e.g., D:\codeql-bundle\ or /opt/codeql-bundle/)
#   4. Set path to codeql executable in the bundle:
#      Windows: CODEQL_CLI_PATH=D:\codeql-bundle\codeql\codeql.exe
#      Linux/Mac: CODEQL_CLI_PATH=/opt/codeql-bundle/codeql/codeql
#
#   Why Bundle instead of CLI-only?
#   - Bundle includes: CLI + extractors + standard queries
#   - CLI-only: Just the executable (will fail with "no extractor" error)
#
# DOCKER MODE: Leave CODEQL_CLI_PATH unset/commented to use Docker
#   - No CodeQL installation required
#   - Uses official image: ghcr.io/github/codeql-cli2:latest
#   - Requires Docker to be running
#   - Recommended for beginners or quick testing
#
# Uncomment and set the path below to enable LOCAL MODE:
# CODEQL_CLI_PATH=/absolute/path/to/codeql-bundle/codeql/codeql

# Optional: ID or name of a running Docker container to reuse for CodeQL analysis
# If not set, ephemeral containers will be created with docker run --rm
# To use a running container:
#   1. Start a container: docker run -d --name codeql-server ghcr.io/github/codeql-cli2:latest tail -f /dev/null
#   2. Set this to the container name or ID
# CODEQL_CONTAINER_ID=codeql-server

# Optional defaults used by tests or local experimentation
# CODEQL_DATABASE_PATH=/path/to/database
# CODEQL_QUERIES_PATH=/path/to/queries

# LLM API Keys (required for agent)
# Uncomment and set the one you're using:

# For OpenAI (GPT-4, GPT-3.5, etc.)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

# For Anthropic (Claude)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
